      "type": "raw",
      "eyebrow": "The AI",
      "heading": "Two AI companies read what you send.",
      "html": "<p class=\"site-words\">When you walk a site and send messages, photos and voice notes in WhatsApp, Quickler uses AI to understand your replies, describe photos and draft your Record. That work is done by <strong>Anthropic</strong> (the Claude models) and <strong>OpenAI</strong>. Both receive the messages, transcripts, photos and uploaded documents needed for the job. A person on your side checks and approves every Record before it goes out.</p>\n<p class=\"site-words\">Voice notes are turned into text by <strong>ElevenLabs</strong> first. If that fails or comes back empty, <strong>OpenAI</strong> does it instead.</p>\n<p class=\"site-words\"><strong>What they say about your data.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"site-words\"><strong>Anthropic.</strong> On training, Anthropic says: \"By default, we will not use your inputs or outputs from our commercial products\" to train its models. On retention, for its API it says it automatically deletes inputs and outputs from its backend within 30 days, with exceptions such as legal requirements or safety enforcement. Sources: <a href=\"https://privacy.claude.com/en/articles/7996868-is-my-data-used-for-model-training\" rel=\"noopener\">training</a> and <a href=\"https://privacy.claude.com/en/articles/7996866-how-long-do-you-store-my-organization-s-data\" rel=\"noopener\">retention</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"site-words\"><strong>OpenAI.</strong> OpenAI says data sent to its API is not used to train or improve its models unless you opt in. By default its API abuse-monitoring logs are kept for up to 30 days. Its speech-to-text endpoint is listed as not used for training and with no abuse-monitoring retention. Source: <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data\" rel=\"noopener\">OpenAI, your data</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"site-words\"><strong>ElevenLabs.</strong> It is listed in our <a href=\"/pages/privacy.html\">privacy policy</a> as a speech-to-text provider. We have not yet checked and published its training and retention terms, so we make no claim about them here.</p>\n<p class=\"site-words\">These are the providers' own published statements, as read on 5 November 2026. We cannot audit their systems, only choose providers whose terms say this.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "raw",
      "eyebrow": "Everyone else",
      "heading": "Who else touches it.",
      "html": "<p class=\"site-words\">Our <a href=\"/pages/privacy.html\">privacy policy</a> lists every company that handles data for us and why, including: Hetzner (hosting), Twilio and Meta (WhatsApp delivery), Cloudflare (sits in front of the dashboard), Resend (email delivery), Sentry (error monitoring), Backblaze (encrypted off-site backups), GoCardless (billing) and map and weather services that receive a Record's location.</p>\n<p class=\"site-words\">Two of those deserve plain words. Cloudflare can see the pages and Records shown at app.quickler.co, because all traffic passes through its network. Sentry error reports can incidentally include fragments of what a person typed when something goes wrong.</p>"
    },
