      "type": "raw",
      "eyebrow": "Where it lives",
      "heading": "Servers in Europe.",
      "html": "<p class=\"site-words\">The product and its databases run on Hetzner servers in Finland (Hetzner Online GmbH is German). A continuous encrypted copy for disaster recovery is held with Backblaze in the United States, and backups are kept for 30 days. Some of the companies above are American, and our privacy policy sets out the legal mechanism for each transfer.</p>\n<p class=\"site-words\">Data is encrypted in transit (HTTPS). We do not claim encryption at rest on our own servers.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "raw",
      "eyebrow": "Tracking",
      "heading": "What watches you, and what does not.",
      "html": "<p class=\"site-words\">The emails we checked, the welcome email and the Record-ready email, contain no images and no tracking.</p>\n<p class=\"site-words\">On the marketing site, Google measurement runs without cookies and with IP anonymisation until you choose. Cookie-based Google analytics and Microsoft Clarity (heatmaps and session replay) load only after you accept cookies. Microsoft Clarity is never loaded on Record pages, history pages or shared Record links. We also use Google Ads conversion measurement on the marketing site, so we are not free of advertising tools ourselves. Details are in our <a href=\"/pages/cookies.html\">cookie policy</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"site-words\">We got this wrong once. In August 2026 session replay was switched on for our own test system without asking for consent. It held no real customer data and was fixed within about 53 hours, and we logged it in our breach record. We now block analytics on every page that shows a Record.</p>"
